    "description": {
      "type": "/type/text",
      "value": "Since the French Revolution the influence of woman in Europe has DECLINED in proportion as she has increased her rights and claims; and the \"emancipation of woman,\" insofar as it is desired and demanded by women themselves (and not only by masculine shallow-pates), thus proves to be a remarkable symptom of the increased weakening and deadening of the most womanly instincts."
